  "term": "behavioral finance",
  "definition": "Behavioral finance is an area of finance that examines how psychological biases and emotions influence investment decisions and the allocation of assets. In the packet, it is described through effects such as regret, where remorse and hesitation can shape choices and lead investors to avoid recognizing losses or to miss opportunities.",
